"""
Real C# production InputData/VPCIData cases, for differential testing of
legacy_pci_engine.py against the actual VPCI_Application.exe (see
test_legacy_pci_golden.py). This fixture is EXTRACTED data, not written by
hand -- see tools/extract_production_join.ps1 +
tools/csv_to_production_fixture.py to regenerate it.

Source: Adman L3001 Rathangan Jan23 PCI.accdb (InputData INNER JOIN VPCIData ON Road, Chainage=ChainageStart)
Extracted: 2026-10-06, READ-ONLY, from a local copy of the production
backup -- the production file itself was never opened directly; see the
project's production-validation deliverable report for the full safety
chain (local copy, size-verified, locked read-only, never touched again).

1315 rows -- every InputData row in this database joined 1:1 with a
VPCIData row (zero orphans either direction), i.e. this is the FULL rated,
non-skipped population of this database, not a cherry-picked sample.

`labels` is {storage_key: selected_descriptor} exactly as
legacy_pci_adapter.build_cells_from_labels() expects -- i.e. literally what
InputData stored for that sample unit's 17 combo-box selections.

`expected_*` fields come directly from the matching VPCIData row -- see
legacy_pci_engine.py's module docstring for the column-name swap this
extraction already accounts for (VPCIData's un-suffixed distress columns
hold Quantity; its "...Quantity"-suffixed columns hold DeductValue -- the
opposite of what their names say, confirmed against this exact data). There
is no stored maxDeduct/finalDeduct column in VPCIData; finalDeduct is exactly
recoverable as 100-PCI (not independent information, see the deliverable
report), so it is not duplicated here.
"""
